<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.9.4: Expressions in Standard Form</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01892</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.9.4: Expressions in Standard Form</md:title>
    <md:uuid>19e9e774-3760-4cfb-94f1-27d3a8bfc41b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>For each expression, write an equivalent expression in <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">standard form</term>. Show your reasoning.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\((2x+5)(x+1)\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para> \(2x^2+7x+5\). The diagram shows that\((2x+5)(x+1)=2x \cdot x+2x \cdot 1+5 \cdot x+5 \cdot 1\). Adding this
    together gives \(2x^2+7x+5\) in standard form.</para>
  <table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis"/>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(2x\)</entry>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(5\)</entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
        <entry>\(2x^2\)</entry>
        <entry>\(5x\)</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(1\)</entry>
        <entry>\(2x\)</entry>
        <entry>\(5\)</entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
    <problem>
      
      <para>\((x-2)(x+2)\)</para>
      <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(x^2-4\). \((x+2)(x-2)=x^2+(-2x)+2x+(-4)=x^2-4\).The diagram also shows that \((x+2)(x-2)=x^2-4\).</para>
    <table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
      <thead>
        <row>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis"/>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
          <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(2\)</entry>
        </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
          <entry>\(x^2\)</entry>
          <entry>\(2x\)</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(-2\)</entry>
          <entry>\(-2x\)</entry>
          <entry>\(-4\)</entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table></solution></exercise>
  </example></section>
</content>
</document>
